  "articleBody": "When you're diving into an interior restoration, it's easy to trip up on a few common hurdles. But with a little foresight, you can sail right past them! Here are some mistakes to watch out for: \n1. Unclear Scope: Don't start without a crystal-clear idea of what you want. If your vision is fuzzy, the project can quickly go off track. Make sure you and your contractor are on the same page from day one. \n2. Late Material Selection: Waiting until the last minute to pick out tiles, cabinets, or paint colors can cause major delays. Custom items often have long lead times, so choose early to keep things moving. \n3. Underestimating Timelines: Interior projects, especially larger ones, take time – often 3-9 months for overall completion, with planning alone taking 2-6 weeks. Be realistic about the schedule. \n4. Not Planning Room Access: Think about how the work will impact your daily life. Will you need to move out, or can you cordon off the area? Plan for access so the crew can work efficiently and safely. \n5. Skipping Professional Help for Complexities: If your project involves multiple trades, structural changes, or custom work, trying to DIY or hire inexperienced help can lead to bigger problems. A qualified professional, like HH Remodeling LLC, brings coordinated design, procurement, and installation management to the table, ensuring quality and saving you headaches. Get in touch early to ensure your project avoids these pitfalls!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
